Track 2: "Why Did You Burn the MiniDisc in the Hearth?"
- Story & Context: During a rain-soaked November rehearsal in 1996, cornetist Maeve Sterling caught her sound engineer attempting to digitally clean and master their analog session using a sleek, cold Japanese MiniDisc recorder. Furious that the sterile digital format erased the microtonal scrape of their space-rock tonewheels, she hurled the plastic disc straight into the studio's cast-iron woodstove, where it melted with a foul stench of burnt polymer and cedar ash. They immediately tracked this confessional, tear-stained ballad in one take around the glowing embers, with the organ's lower manual groaning under an agonizing, dragging tempo as Maeve whispered into her cornet's bell, "you loved the clean quartz digital shine, but I need the grit of burning stones."
